    description: "FOUND BY THE WI-zazul VALIDATION COHORT 2026-08-02, on the 9-repo fresh\nsubstrate, using INV-karud's own realizability probe.\n\nTHE NUMBERS. Non-realizable sink matches (the emitted (lang, module, name) does\nnot exist in the catalog, though the NAME does for that language):\n    before WI-zazul: 51        after WI-zazul: 43\nWI-zazul removed exactly its own 8 substring matches and nothing else. The 43\nsurvivors split into two shapes that are NOT substring matching:\n\n  30  the emitted module slot holds a FILE PATH, not a module\n        18  go          logging.go                              Log\n         8  javascript  .../iframeresizer/iframeResizer.contentWindow.js  warn\n         1  javascript  src/pretix/static/d3/d3.v6.js           log\n         1  javascript  src/pretix/static/d3/d3-dispatch.v2.js  get\n         1  javascript  lib/application.js                      debug\n         1  python      hack/setup/scripts/generate-versions-from-gomod.py  run\n  13  go   net/http  Do   -- a real package, and the match is CORRECT\n        (the catalog entry is net/http.Client and Client.Do does perform\n        network IO). The emitted module records the PACKAGE while the catalog\n        records PACKAGE.TYPE, so no consumer can verify the match by lookup.\n        This is a labelling/provenance defect, not a wrong match, and it should\n        be adjudicated separately from the file-path class.\n\nWHY THIS MATTERS BEYOND THE COUNT, and it is a correction to WI-zazul's filing.\nINV-karud's two headline examples were d3's `log` (the LOGARITHM reported as a\nconsole.log sink) and net/http/httptest.NewRequest. WI-zazul attributed BOTH to\nsubstring module matching and fixed that mechanism. Only httptest was a\nsubstring defect. d3's `log` IS STILL PRESENT after the fix, because `console`\nnever substring-matched a file path -- that flow is matched through the\nNO-MODULE-HINT path (gate_named_entry + ambiguous_names), not through\n_module_matches at all. The filing was wrong on the SCOPE AXIS (L1): every\ncount in it was real, and the generalisation to one mechanism was not.\n\nCONSEQUENCE FOR INV-karud: it stays violated, and its root cause is now known to\nbe at least two distinct mechanisms, of which only one has been fixed.\n\nINVESTIGATION SHAPE (not implemented). Establish where the file path enters the\nmodule slot: is _extract_module_hint returning a path for these symbol ids, or\nis the analyzer emitting a path-shaped module in the id itself? Those need\nopposite fixes. The 18 go/logging.go/Log flows are the cheapest probe -- one\nrepo, one file, one name. Do NOT assume the JS and Go cases share a cause; the\nsubstring bug looked uniform too and turned out to be Go-and-JS-only for\nlanguage-coverage reasons.\n\nDO NOT close this by widening _module_matches. That predicate was just tightened\nfor good reason; a file path is not a module and making it match one would\nrestore the class WI-zazul removed."  # a957
    fields: {}  # a957
